---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import GradientDivider from "../../components/GradientDivider.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Loomey Terms of Service"
  description="Terms of Service for the Loomey reading, library, social, reporting, and digital reading application."
>
  <main class="home-page">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Loomey Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="hero-text">Last updated: October 2026</p>
    </section>

    <GradientDivider />

    <section class="policy-grid">
      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Agreement to These Terms</h2>

        <p>
          These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of Loomey, a
          Voxiverse application for organizing books, tracking reading activity,
          setting reading goals, reviewing reading statistics, using digital
          reading tools, participating in social reading features, and accessing
          other reading-related experiences provided through the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          By downloading, accessing, or using Loomey, you agree to these Terms.
          If you do not agree with these Terms, you should discontinue use of
          Loomey.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Using Loomey</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey provides tools for managing a personal reading library and
          related reading activity. Features may include books, reading sessions,
          notes, quotes, reviews, reading insights, goals, missions, streaks,
          achievements, reading lists, EPUB reading, recommendations, sprints,
          buddy reading, challenges, bingos, profiles, report tools, and other
          reading-related features.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for how you use Loomey and for the information,
          files, text, images, ratings, comments, messages, profile details,
          reading records, and other content you choose to add, import, create,
          submit, or share through the application.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Your Content</h2>

        <p>
          You retain ownership of the original content and information you add to
          Loomey, including your library records, notes, quotes, reviews, reading
          insights, reading lists, goal information, imported EPUB files,
          comments, messages, challenge submissions, profile information, and
          other material you create or provide.
        </p>

        <p>
          By using Loomey, you permit the application and the systems supporting
          it to store, process, display, synchronize, transmit, and organize that
          content as reasonably necessary to provide the features you choose to
          use.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not claim ownership of your original content merely
          because you use Loomey.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Accounts & Sign In</h2>

        <p>
          Certain Loomey features use account information and authentication.
          Loomey supports Sign in with Apple and may store account-related
          information such as your Apple user identifier, display name, and email
          when Apple provides it.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for maintaining access to the Apple account and
          device credentials associated with your Loomey use. You may not attempt
          to access another person's account, impersonate another user, or bypass
          authentication or account protections.
        </p>

        <p>
          Sign in with Apple and related Apple account services are also subject
          to Apple's own terms, policies, and service availability.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Synchronization & Cloud Storage</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey stores app data using Apple technologies including SwiftData and
          CloudKit, and may synchronize supported records through a private iCloud
          container associated with the app.
        </p>

        <p>
          Synchronization may depend on your iCloud account, device state,
          network connection, available storage, Apple service availability, and
          other technical conditions. Continuous or immediate synchronization
          cannot be guaranteed.
        </p>

        <p>
          You remain responsible for reviewing information that is especially
          important to you and for keeping separate copies when you consider that
          necessary.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Book Search, Recommendations & Enrichment</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey may send search terms, book titles, authors, library context,
          ratings, reading-session information, preferences, tags, genres,
          tropes, moods, and other relevant reading context to Voxiverse services
          in order to provide book search results, recommendations, summaries,
          metadata enrichment, and related reading features.
        </p>

        <p>
          Results produced through these services may rely on third-party book
          information, external data sources, automated processing, or generated
          content. Book metadata, summaries, recommendations, ratings, page
          counts, classifications, release information, and similar results may
          be incomplete, inaccurate, or unavailable.
        </p>

        <p>
          You should use your own judgment before relying on recommendation or
          enrichment results for purchasing, research, accessibility, academic,
          or other important decisions.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Reading Insights & Generated Reviews</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey may process reading insights and related book context through
          Voxiverse services to generate summaries, reviews, classifications, or
          other reading-related output.
        </p>

        <p>
          Generated output may not reflect your exact meaning, may contain
          mistakes, and may require editing before you save, publish, or rely on
          it. You remain responsible for reviewing any generated content before
          using it as your own final work.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>EPUB Files & Digital Reading</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey allows you to import and read EPUB files and may store EPUB file
          data, bookmarks, highlights, annotations, reader settings, and reading
          position information as part of your library.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for ensuring that you have the right to possess,
          import, copy, read, annotate, and store any EPUB file you add to
          Loomey. Loomey does not grant you rights to copyrighted books or other
          digital publications that you do not already have.
        </p>

        <p>
          File compatibility, formatting, embedded media, navigation, metadata,
          and rendering can vary between EPUB files and cannot be guaranteed for
          every publication.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Goodreads Imports & Data Portability</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey may allow you to import library data from Goodreads-compatible
          CSV files and to export portions of your Loomey library.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for reviewing imported records, duplicates,
          statuses, dates, ratings, and other information before relying on them.
          Import and export tools may not preserve every field, formatting choice,
          relationship, or piece of metadata from an external service.
        </p>

        <p>
          Goodreads is a third-party service and is not operated by Voxiverse.
          References to Goodreads describe compatibility with user-provided data
          and do not imply sponsorship or affiliation.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Social & Community Features</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey may include social reading features such as buddy reading,
          groups, chats, sprint rooms, leaderboards, challenge feeds, comments,
          likes, announcements, profiles, submissions, and other shared spaces.
        </p>

        <p>
          Content you choose to post in shared features may be visible to other
          participants. You are responsible for what you post and for respecting
          the privacy, rights, and safety of other users.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may not use community features to harass, threaten, impersonate,
          defraud, spam, exploit, or unlawfully target another person, or to share
          content you do not have the right to distribute.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Challenge Submissions & Automated Review</h2>

        <p>
          Some Loomey challenge features may allow you to submit text, photos, or
          other evidence and may use automated systems or Voxiverse services to
          evaluate whether a submission appears to meet challenge requirements.
        </p>

        <p>
          Automated validation may be imperfect and does not guarantee that every
          submission will be interpreted correctly. Voxiverse may adjust,
          disable, or change challenge validation methods as the feature evolves.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Reading Sprints, Buddy Groups & Live Features</h2>

        <p>
          Live or near-live features may use network connections and Voxiverse
          backend services for rooms, group activity, chat, progress updates,
          leaderboards, or similar functionality.
        </p>

        <p>
          These features may experience delays, dropped connections, unavailable
          rooms, duplicate events, missing updates, or temporary service outages.
          Live state and leaderboard information should not be treated as
          guaranteed or permanent records.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Notifications</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey may request permission to send notifications for reading events,
          timers, reminders, sprint activity, report conversations, or other app
          features.
        </p>

        <p>
          Delivery depends on device settings, notification permissions, system
          conditions, and Apple services. Voxiverse cannot guarantee that a
          notification will arrive at a particular time or at all.
        </p>

        <p>
          You are responsible for using in-app information rather than relying
          solely on notifications for anything important or time-sensitive.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Feedback, Reports & Private Support Conversations</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey includes the Voxiverse reporting system for bug reports, beta
          feedback, and feature requests. Reports may include information you
          intentionally provide, attachments, report details, and automatically
          collected diagnostic information such as app version, build number,
          device model, iOS version, locale, time zone, and screen context.
        </p>

        <p>
          Submitted reports may be stored locally in Loomey and transmitted to
          Voxiverse through CloudKit. Voxiverse may invite you to a private
          conversation connected to a submitted report when follow-up is needed.
        </p>

        <p>
          Submitting feedback, an idea, or a feature request does not create an
          obligation for Voxiverse to implement, publish, compensate, or provide
          attribution for that suggestion.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey depends in part on Apple frameworks and services and may also
          communicate with Voxiverse backend services and external sources used
          to locate, enrich, or verify book information.
        </p>

        <p>
          Third-party and external services may change, limit access, return
          incorrect information, become unavailable, or apply their own terms
          and policies. Voxiverse does not control those external services and
          cannot guarantee their continued availability.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Acceptable Use</h2>

        <p>
          You may use Loomey for lawful personal, reading, organizational, and
          community purposes. You may not use Loomey in a way that violates
          applicable law, infringes another person's rights, interferes with the
          operation of the application, abuses community spaces, or attempts to
          gain unauthorized access to Voxiverse systems or services.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may not attempt to bypass security controls, manipulate service
          requests, disrupt backend systems, distribute malicious content,
          scrape or overload protected services, or use Loomey as part of
          unlawful or fraudulent activity.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Copyright & Intellectual Property</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey, including its software, interface, design, branding, graphics,
          original components, documentation, and other Voxiverse-created
          materials, is owned by Voxiverse or its respective rights holders and
          is protected by applicable intellectual property laws.
        </p>

        <p>
          These Terms do not transfer ownership of Loomey or Voxiverse
          intellectual property to you. You are granted a limited right to use
          the application for its intended purpose while these Terms remain in
          effect.
        </p>

        <p>
          Books, covers, descriptions, quotations, EPUB publications, external
          metadata, and other third-party materials remain subject to the rights
          of their respective owners.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Availability & Changes</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey may be updated, redesigned, expanded, or modified over time.
          Features may be added, changed, temporarily unavailable, limited,
          replaced, or removed as the application develops.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not guarantee that every feature, service, social space,
          external integration, backend endpoint, or synchronization capability
          will remain available permanently or operate without interruption.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Beta & Developing Features</h2>

        <p>
          Some Loomey features may be introduced or provided while still under
          active development or testing.
        </p>

        <p>
          Developing features may contain bugs, behave unexpectedly, change
          substantially, produce incomplete results, or be removed. Feedback you
          submit about these features may be used to investigate problems and
          improve Loomey.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Data Loss</h2>

        <p>
          Reasonable care is taken in developing and maintaining Loomey, but no
          software, local database, cloud synchronization system, imported file,
          backend service, or networked feature can guarantee protection against
          every possible failure, corrupted record, accidental deletion,
          synchronization conflict, service interruption, or device problem.
        </p>

        <p>
          You should maintain independent copies of information or files that are
          especially important to you when appropriate.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>

        <p>
          Loomey is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis to the extent
          permitted by applicable law.
        </p>

        <p>
          Voxiverse does not guarantee that Loomey will always be uninterrupted,
          error-free, secure, compatible with every device, accurate in every
          recommendation or generated result, or able to preserve every imported
          file, social update, notification, external record, or synchronized
          item without interruption.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>

        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Voxiverse will not
          be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or similar
          damages resulting from your use of Loomey or your inability to use the
          application.
        </p>

        <p>
          This includes losses related to unavailable books or metadata,
          incorrect recommendations or generated content, imported data,
          unavailable EPUB files, synchronization issues, community activity,
          service outages, lost progress, delayed notifications, or reliance on
          information provided through external or automated services.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Suspension or Termination</h2>

        <p>
          Access to certain Loomey or Voxiverse services may be restricted,
          moderated, or terminated when reasonably necessary to protect users,
          community spaces, application infrastructure, Voxiverse systems, or
          third parties from abuse, unlawful activity, fraud, security threats,
          or serious violations of these Terms.
        </p>

        <p>
          You may stop using Loomey at any time.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Privacy</h2>

        <p>
          Your use of Loomey is also subject to the Loomey Privacy Policy, which
          explains how information associated with the application is handled.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Privacy Policy should be reviewed alongside these Terms because
          both documents apply to your use of Loomey.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/legal/loomey/privacy" class="policy-link">
            View Loomey Privacy Policy
          </a>
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>

        <p>
          These Terms may be updated from time to time to reflect changes to
          Loomey, Voxiverse services, app functionality, legal requirements, or
          the way features are provided.
        </p>

        <p>
          When these Terms are updated, the revised version will be published on
          this page and the last updated date will be changed accordingly.
          Continued use of Loomey after updated Terms become effective
          constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms where permitted by law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Severability</h2>

        <p>
          If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid or
          unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue to apply to the
          fullest extent permitted by law.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="policy-card">
        <h2>Contact</h2>

        <p>
          If you have questions about these Terms of Service or about Loomey,
          you can contact Voxiverse.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="/contact" class="contact-button">Contact</a>
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .policy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    padding-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-card {
    background: var(--surface-standard);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .policy-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  .policy-card h2 {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--heading-small);
  }

  .policy-card p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .policy-card a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .policy-link {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--accent-periwinkle) !important;
  }

  .policy-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .contact-button {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--accent-periwinkle);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(242, 239, 231, 0.12);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition:
      transform 0.2s ease,
      border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .contact-button:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--accent-periwinkle);
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .policy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .policy-card {
      padding: 1.25rem;
      border-radius: 20px;
    }
  }
</style>